class.description:
[InputMapSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"input_map"[/code]: it stores the keys, mouse buttons and joypad inputs the player bound to the actions of the project, loads them when the game starts and applies them to [InputMap] (in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SERVERS], before the [SceneTree] exists). Sensitivity, inversion, vibration and the global deadzone are a separate domain, see [InputSettingsServer].
An event slot is addressed by action, device ([enum InputMapAction.InputDevice]: keyboard, mouse or gamepad) and slot. A rebinding menu with the columns "Keyboard 1", "Keyboard 2" and "Gamepad" waits for the next input of the player and calls [method rebind] with the slot of the column; the device follows from the event. [method find_conflicts] tells which other actions use the event already, so the game can swap, clear or refuse. [method get_event_label] gives the text for the buttons of the menu.
The settings resource is an [InputMapSettings] with one [InputMapAction] row per slot. The defaults are the [InputMap] of the project settings when the game starts, so [method reset_action] and [method reset_all] give back the bindings of the project. Built-in [code]ui_*[/code] actions are left out unless [member ProjectSettings.settings/input_map/include_builtin_actions] is [code]true[/code].
When the file is loaded, the saved rows replace the bindings of their action. Actions added to the project since the file was saved keep their project bindings; saved actions that the project no longer has are skipped with a warning. Applying replaces the key, mouse button and joypad events of each action; other event types (touch, MIDI, ...) stay.
The file is [code]user://settings/input_map.ini[/code] by default and stores every event as readable text such as [code]Key:Ctrl+S[/code] or [code]JoypadMotion:LeftX+[/code] (see [InputMapAction]). It can also be stored as JSON or as CSV with one row per event ([member ProjectSettings.settings/storage/format]).
All methods below change the pending settings: in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_IMMEDIATE] a change reaches [InputMap] at once and is saved at the end of the frame; in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_MANUAL] it waits for [method SettingsServer.apply].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var waiting_action = &""
var waiting_slot = 0

func _on_jump_key_button_pressed():
	waiting_action = &"jump"
	waiting_slot = 0

func _input(event):
	if waiting_action.is_empty() or not event.is_pressed():
		return
	if InputMapAction.get_event_device(event) == InputMapAction.INPUT_DEVICE_MAX:
		return # Mouse motion, touch, ...
	get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()
	for other in InputMapSettingsServer.find_conflicts(event, waiting_action):
		InputMapSettingsServer.clear_event(other, InputMapAction.get_event_device(event), 0)
	InputMapSettingsServer.rebind(waiting_action, event, waiting_slot)
	$JumpKeyButton.text = InputMapSettingsServer.get_event_label(event)
	waiting_action = &""
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
private StringName _waitingAction = "";
private int _waitingSlot = 0;

private void OnJumpKeyButtonPressed()
{
    _waitingAction = "jump";
    _waitingSlot = 0;
}

public override void _Input(InputEvent @event)
{
    if (_waitingAction.IsEmpty || !@event.IsPressed())
    {
        return;
    }
    if (InputMapAction.GetEventDevice(@event) == InputMapAction.InputDevice.Max)
    {
        return; // Mouse motion, touch, ...
    }
    GetViewport().SetInputAsHandled();
    foreach (string other in InputMapSettingsServer.FindConflicts(@event, _waitingAction))
    {
        InputMapSettingsServer.ClearEvent(other, InputMapAction.GetEventDevice(@event), 0);
    }
    InputMapSettingsServer.Rebind(_waitingAction, @event, _waitingSlot);
    GetNode<Button>("JumpKeyButton").Text = InputMapSettingsServer.GetEventLabel(@event);
    _waitingAction = "";
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
